# Reference
- Concepts: Tranek,
  https://github.com/tranek/GASDocumentation
- Code: `C:\Game\Arena\Narxim-GAS-Example\Source\GAS_Example`.
  When they differ, follow Narxim.
- Before writing an ability, an attribute set, or
  Enhanced Input for an ability, read the matching
  Narxim file and follow that procedure.
- Narxim is Unreal 5.6. This project is 5.8.1.
  Copy the procedure, not the engine version.

# Names
- Ability classes use the prefix `JoA_GAS_`.
- Name an attribute set for the stats it holds,
  suffix `Set`. Health and attack live on `CombatSet`,
  not `JoA_AttributeSet`.
- Numeric stats are a `UAttributeSet` with
  `ATTRIBUTE_ACCESSORS`.

# Where the ASC lives
- `UAbilitySystemComponent` and its attribute sets
  stay on the figure. One player fields several
  figures, so the ASC does not go on `APlayerState`.
- Server: `PossessedBy()`, then
  `InitAbilityActorInfo` with the figure as owner
  and avatar. Same order as Narxim
  `Characters/CharacterBase.cpp`.
- Client: when the owning player state replicates,
  not in `BeginPlay`.

# Abilities and input
- A new ability is its own `JoA_GAS_` class, in the
  style of
  `AbilitySystem/GameplayAbilities/CustomGameplayAbility`.
- The ability holds the `UInputAction`. Bind it on
  the Enhanced Input component in `OnGiveAbility`.
  Clear that binding when the ability is removed.
- Wait for input with an ability task, as in
  `AbilitySystem/AbilityTasks/AbilityTask_WaitEnhancedInputEvent`.
- Do not bind gameplay actions as one-off test keys
  on the player controller.

# Attributes and effects
- Split attribute sets by concern. Replicate them
  with `DOREPLIFETIME_WITH_PARAMS_FAST` and
  `bIsPushBased`, as in
  `AttributeSets/HealthAttributeSet.cpp`.
- Clamp in `PreAttributeChange()` and in
  `PostGameplayEffectExecute()`.
- Change stats through a `UGameplayEffect`. Damage
  and healing go through a meta attribute and a
  server execution, not a SetByCaller write onto
  Health.
- The server grants starting sets, abilities,
  effects, and tags from one initialization struct.
  See `AbilitySystem/Data/AbilitySystemData.h` and
  `InitializeAbilitySystemData`.
- A turn-based damage-over-time or buff follows
  `AbilitySystem/GameplayEffects/TurnBased`, not a
  real-time periodic effect.

# Tags and flow
- Use `FGameplayTag` and `FNativeGameplayTag` for
  turn phase, status, and cancel.
- No game logic, timers, or phase polling in
  `Tick()` or `NativeTick()`.
- Drive actions and UI from gameplay events, tags,
  and attribute change delegates. Wait inside a
  `UAbilityTask`.

# Do not copy from Narxim
- Iris replicates the board, cells, and figure
  state. GAS attribute data stays on the push model
  above.
- Do not set a 100 Hz net update frequency.
- Do not bring movement, CommonUI, Model View
  ViewModel, or the AGRPRO plugin.
